{"title":"2005 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> be a Pythagorean triple, <i>i.e.</i>, a triplet of positive integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfdf6560d670d1b011d72c3acf7c3a7cc62bdc1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${a}^2+{b}^2={c}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5dc37a209ceca7de11cfc90b70adb9f116e56c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c/a + c/b)^2 &gt; 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"19\" />.</li>\n<li>Prove that there does not exist any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which we can find a Pythagorean triple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92e61d99b0277472a87234dbcf495cdda75c2dd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c/a + c/b)^2 = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"21\" />.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>We have</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/8/f688db669acea4ece5f3015d0fa5eb24fd311aa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac ca + \\frac cb\\right)^2 = \\frac{c^2}{a^2} + 2\\frac{c^2}{ab} + \\frac{c^2}{b^2} = \\frac{a^2 + b^2}{a^2} + 2\\frac{a^2 + b^2}{ab} + \\frac{a^2+b^2}{b^2} = 2 + \\left(\\frac{a^2}{b^2} + \\frac{b^2}{a^2}\\right) + 2\\left(\\frac ab + \\frac ba\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"721\" height=\"43\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM\">AM-GM</a>, we have \n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/5417e979304954f3ef16b298538e5a2201818541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + \\frac 1x &gt; 2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"84\" height=\"37\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Positive\">positive</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real number</a> not equal to one.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397fd7b1f33bdbf6ee27a83d1bcee42d222cb331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0bac0e1acd0b0c8ecc64ac559659859a25195dc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\not\\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af40dd462cfac9a98f63c84a474236829d0b3c25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\neq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/9/6091689ed54951be149c724e9561386fe68c367d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac ab \\neq 1\\implies \\frac{a^2}{b^2}\\neq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"149\" height=\"39\" />. Therefore, \n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/8875d13ec247a30fce5c1da3b64c558e122592e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac ca + \\frac cb\\right)^2 &gt; 2 + 2 + 2(2) = 8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"232\" height=\"36\" /></dd></dl>\n<ul><li>Now since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/f/e2f4cf10c7e7d41b87472b8b15c73ef062771de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c/a + c/b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> is a rational number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9868fbf23bed343deebad0af0b21b1ceef79889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p/q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers. Now if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/a/a4a5152f1331ec065ee52bdfdb39cdd852f3a0f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2/q^2=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9868fbf23bed343deebad0af0b21b1ceef79889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p/q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> must also be an integer. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10c5f80230ede9d825fe760aa697707bde4bc924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c(a+b)/ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" /> must be an integer.</li></ul>\n<p>Now every pythagorean triple can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/987edc025807d9196aa23c34c898b2f8e1da9e39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2mn, m^2-n^2, m^2+n^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"192\" height=\"19\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive integers. Thus one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> must be even. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are both even, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is even too. Factors of 4 can be cancelled from the numerator and the denominator(since every time one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> increase by a factor of 2, they all increase by a factor of 2) repeatedly until one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, and we can continue from there. Thus the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c3ec31f0ae75b638f255d25454d3efa57dc8a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2-n^2$\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> term is odd, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is odd. Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> are odd, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> is even. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10c5f80230ede9d825fe760aa697707bde4bc924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c(a+b)/ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" /> is not an integer. Now we have reached a contradiction, and thus there does not exist any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which we can find a Pythagorean triple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92e61d99b0277472a87234dbcf495cdda75c2dd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c/a + c/b)^2 = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Canadian_MO\" title=\"2005 Canadian MO\">2005 Canadian MO</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Canadian_MO\" title=\"2005 Canadian MO\">2005 Canadian MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Canadian_MO_Problems\" title=\"2005 Canadian MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018050959\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 282/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 756/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 40/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8883/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   20.665      1 Template:CanadaMO_box\n100.00%   20.665      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3629:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018050959 and revision id 28003. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}